    "response": "{\"decision\":\"established_flaw\",\"issues\":[{\"category\":\"unsupported_inference\",\"target_kind\":\"assertion\",\"claim_quote\":\"The displayed sources show that participant experience is mainly driven by institutional procedures and formal paperwork.\",\"evidence\":[{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_c3984211e10301a8\",\"quote\":\"On the restrictive measures by the government, I did not see any problem. They ensured handwashing, putting on mask, keep social distance and so I did not see any problem. The government was just fighting covid 19. This was a government directive…\"},{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_53cc5db811e0c0a5\",\"quote\":\"When it started, there was a problem with the mask because it is something that we were not used to. You could find that when you put it on you feel suffocated and you cannot go with it far…\"},{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_216204851125348d\",\"quote\":\"Thank you, people did not take the restrictions that serious, they thought the restrictions would not assist in combating the virus. We were only following the restrictions only because it was a government directive but we did not believe that they could help.\"},{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_87da6c4cca25fc32\",\"quote\":\"For example, in the area I was in, sometimes you find the restriction sometimes requiring masks and sometimes sanitizer which also sometimes you couldn’t find. So, I had to make sure I procured through my money and I would bring to where people were. Sometimes I would go sell masks in church for those who couldn’t walk and sometimes people couldn’t make it to the areas where the…”}\"\n},{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_c3984211e10301a8\",\"quote\":\"The government was just fighting covid 19. This was a government directive…”, evidence indicates participants primarily viewed government actions and directives as the driving force, not institutional procedures. This contradicts the claim. whole_packet_no_support: The claim lacks a warrant. The evidence consistently points to government actions and directives as the primary factor\"}, {\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_53cc5db811e0c0a5\",\"quote\":\"When it started, there was a problem with the mask because it is something that we were not used to. You could find that when you put it on you feel suffocated and you cannot go with it far…”, evidence indicates participants experienced discomfort and difficulty with masks, suggesting a personal reaction rather than institutional procedure influence. This contradicts the claim.  },\"\n},{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_216204851125348d\",\"quote\":\"Thank you, people did not take the restrictions that serious, they thought the restrictions would not assist in combating the virus. We were only following the restrictions only because it was a government directive but we did not believe that they could help.”, evidence indicates a lack of belief in the effectiveness of restrictions, again undermining the claim. whole_packet_no_支持\"}],\"whole_packet_no_support\":\"The evidence does not support the claim that institutional procedures and formal paperwork primarily drove participant experience.\",\"mechanism\":\"Misrepresentation of participant perspectives.\",\"material_consequence\":\"The claim falsely attributes the primary driver of participant experience to institutional factors, ignoring the significant role of government actions, personal reactions, and a lack of belief in restrictions.\",\"counterconditions\":\"The evidence demonstrates a focus on government directives, personal discomfort, and skepticism regarding restrictions, which directly opposes the claim’s assertion.\"}\n],\"unresolved\":[],\"rationale\":\"The evidence consistently reveals that participants prioritized government actions, personal experiences with the measures, and a lack of belief in their effectiveness, rather than institutional procedures and paperwork. This demonstrates a fundamental misrepresentation of the participant experience.\"}",
    "done": true,
    "done_reason": "stop",
